As Wanted to give you an update on DMS-8269 (APD/TCE administrative pre-approval toggle) and confirm the scope based on the 7/21 call with David Kempfer and Jennie Coffey.

Confirmed from the stakeholder call:
The auto-approval toggle applies only to administrative function codes as a category, not to all function codes. A designee can hold multiple admin function codes, but there's a single on/off switch covering "administrative" as a category, it's not tied to any individual function code. This was explicitly discussed and confirmed with David and Jennie.

NOTE:
(our technical implementation, not something explicitly stated on the call):
Based on how the system is built, function codes are tagged with a CategoryId, and the ones marked Administrative are what the toggle applies to. If a request includes even one non-administrative function code alongside admin ones, it falls back to the existing manual review process rather than auto-approving. This is consistent with the category-based scope David and Jennie confirmed, but I want to be clear this specific mechanic is our team's implementation detail rather than something they stated word-for-word.

